{"ts":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"143da6b99c6d50ff73f411da","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Source\\n\\nGitHub #1140: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1140\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nOwn one SDK-level grammar and mutation contract for file and test entries across create, update, dedicated CLI commands, MCP, and public SDK adapters. A comma-bearing value without an explicit leading key must never silently become an unusable path or command. Literal commas remain expressible through explicit keyed or JSON input.\\n\\n## Context integrity\\n\\nProject management equals context management: linked artifacts are executable context, so a successful mutation receipt must not certify a path that cannot resolve or a test command that cannot run solely because an advertised tuple form was parsed as plaintext."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-nc94mk"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1140: reject ambiguous bare comma tuples for linked file and test mutations"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1140 proves that update/create --file and linked-test add paths accept a comma-bearing bare value with no structured key before the first comma, persist the entire tuple as path or command, and return success. The result is a linked file that cannot resolve or a linked test that cannot execute, while TOON rendering can make the corruption look like a valid row."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:sdk","data-integrity","linked-artifacts","parser"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":360},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A shared public SDK parser rejects ambiguous comma-bearing bare file and test entries before mutation with a stable typed refusal and token-efficient keyed/JSON recovery; explicit path= and command= forms preserve literal commas losslessly; create, update, files, test, CLI, SDK, MCP, contracts, completions, and help expose one consistent grammar; health and validation identify legacy corrupted rows without rewriting history; focused unit/integration/packed npm+npx+bun+bunx/temp-workspace acceptance plus literal 100/100/100/100 coverage, docstrings, static, and security gates pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/definition_of_ready","value":"All-status duplicate search remains distinct from the closed structured-key, unknown-key, docs-pair, and delimiter-safe removal fixes; the exact accepted grammar is specified before implementation."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make every linked file and test mutation lossless, executable, and self-describing across SDK and CLI entry points."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Agents can trust a successful linked-artifact write without reopening JSON to detect silent tuple corruption."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Prevents durable false context and permanently unrunnable verification evidence."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"Issue #1140 reports 38 corrupted items across 16 repositories on versions through 2026.8.28, demonstrating a recurring fleet-wide agent UX failure."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"GitHub #1140"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm 2026.8.21 through 2026.8.28; Node 26.5.0; Linux"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run pm update <id> --file \".github/workflows/release.yml,project,the publish step\" or pm test <id> --add \"node scripts/verify.ts,project,120\"; read the item as JSON and observe the entire tuple stored in path or command."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Ambiguous comma tuples refuse before mutation with a stable code and keyed/JSON recovery; explicit keyed inputs preserve legitimate commas."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The mutation exits successfully and stores the complete comma-joined tuple in the first field, creating an unresolved path or unrunnable command."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.21-2026.8.28"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"SDK linked-artifact input grammar and CLI adapters"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":false},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Agents receive successful writes for unusable context and verification evidence; observed across 38 items in 16 repositories."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0v9k","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-fpdk37","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-m0b7h8","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-swie","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T19:16:55.859Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"130374511d4e994919f5acb36af5e2431441d9b1f89afc609d2e4083e8c4f993","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
